00:19:03.751 --> 00:19:05.883
But it has told us
a great deal

274
00:19:05.927 --> 00:19:09.452
about the situation we
find ourselves in.

275
00:19:09.496 --> 00:19:13.239
What he did was not an
impulsive act on his part.

276
00:19:14.370 --> 00:19:15.893
The garden shears.

277
00:19:15.937 --> 00:19:17.678
The towel.

278
00:19:17.721 --> 00:19:19.506
They were planned.

279
00:19:19.549 --> 00:19:23.118
He intended to do
that from the start.

280
00:19:24.337 --> 00:19:27.209
And he intended
to do it to you.

281
00:19:27.253 --> 00:19:28.732
Not to me.

282
00:19:31.605 --> 00:19:33.259
I counted ten cameras.

283
00:19:34.651 --> 00:19:36.392
He said they
were live.

284
00:19:36.436 --> 00:19:40.440
That they're transmitting
images of us right now.

285
00:19:40.483 --> 00:19:45.227
When he instructed us to look at
the pilot camera it seemed to me

286
00:19:45.271 --> 00:19:47.621
as if he were anticipating
that a great number

287
00:19:47.664 --> 00:19:50.667
of people would
be watching us.

288
00:19:50.711 --> 00:19:54.454
They might very well be
watching us right now.

289
00:19:56.717 --> 00:19:59.198
[typing]

290
00:20:05.943 --> 00:20:09.208
[timer ticking]

291
00:20:09.251 --> 00:20:10.644
The clock.

292
00:20:10.687 --> 00:20:12.254
I'm aware of
the clock.

293
00:20:12.298 --> 00:20:13.951
He said five minutes to figure
out the connection.

294
00:20:13.995 --> 00:20:16.737
What the hell is he gonna do
when the five minutes are up?

295
00:20:18.304 --> 00:20:20.262
You don't get it.

296
00:20:20.306 --> 00:20:23.178
You don't get it because you
didn't see the fuckin' movie.

297
00:20:24.223 --> 00:20:25.920
I'll go first.

298
00:20:25.963 --> 00:20:29.358
I'll tell the exact truth to you

299
00:20:29.402 --> 00:20:32.840
and to everyone who is watching.

300
00:20:32.883 --> 00:20:37.236
And I presume that
includes our captor.

301
00:20:37.279 --> 00:20:39.281
He was correct.

302
00:20:39.325 --> 00:20:43.111
I did not tell the
whole story earlier.

303
00:20:43.154 --> 00:20:45.766
My wife is not
at home.

304
00:20:45.809 --> 00:20:49.726
She and my daughter went
away on holiday this morning.

305
00:20:49.770 --> 00:20:52.251
I drove them to
the airport.

306
00:20:52.294 --> 00:20:54.514
And then I went to
the grocery store.

307
00:20:54.557 --> 00:20:58.039
I was in my driveway
unloading groceries

308
00:20:58.082 --> 00:21:02.261
from the back of my car when
a white van drove up.

309
00:21:02.304 --> 00:21:03.436
The driver.

310
00:21:03.479 --> 00:21:07.788
The man who is our
captor got out

311
00:21:07.831 --> 00:21:10.225
and started walking
towards me.

312
00:21:10.269 --> 00:21:14.534
I thought he was lost so I put
down the groceries I had

313
00:21:14.577 --> 00:21:18.059
in my hand so that I
could speak with him.

314
00:21:18.102 --> 00:21:21.105
And then he put a
bag over my head

315
00:21:21.149 --> 00:21:23.630
and knocked the glasses
off my nose.

316
00:21:23.673 --> 00:21:25.806
I could see them on
the pavement.

317
00:21:25.849 --> 00:21:27.808
There were oranges
rolling around

318
00:21:27.851 --> 00:21:31.028
and then down
the driveway.

319
00:21:31.072 --> 00:21:32.334
I couldn't move.

320
00:21:32.378 --> 00:21:35.294
He had me completely
restrained.

321
00:21:35.337 --> 00:21:37.948
And then he manhandled
me into the van.

322
00:21:39.646 --> 00:21:44.041
When we started downhill I
started counting.

323
00:21:48.481 --> 00:21:49.917
Now you.

324
00:21:51.658 --> 00:21:53.790
Ron this will
not work--

325
00:21:53.834 --> 00:21:58.447
We have to get the
fuck out of here.

326
00:21:59.753 --> 00:22:01.363
You were in a
drive-through restaurant,

327
00:22:01.407 --> 00:22:03.974
or you were going to a
drive-through restaurant?

328
00:22:04.018 --> 00:22:07.804
I have two little girls that I
need to see right now.

329
00:22:07.848 --> 00:22:10.764
But you stopped and
got out to what?

330
00:22:10.807 --> 00:22:11.808
To check your tires?

331
00:22:11.852 --> 00:22:13.070
Right now!

332
00:22:13.114 --> 00:22:15.769
Is this part of your
daily routine?

333
00:22:15.812 --> 00:22:17.292
All just 'cause I missed
breakfast.

334
00:22:17.336 --> 00:22:19.033
I wasn't even supposed
to be there.

335
00:22:19.076 --> 00:22:20.730
What do you mean?

336
00:22:20.774 --> 00:22:22.210
I go to Zoop's Chicken Monday,
Tuesday, Wednesday.

337
00:22:22.253 --> 00:22:25.169
Thursday, Friday I go
to Steak and Shake.

338
00:22:25.213 --> 00:22:26.693
One or one-thirty
at the latest.

339
00:22:26.736 --> 00:22:27.911
Everybody knows that.

340
00:22:27.955 --> 00:22:29.435
But this is Saturday.

341
00:22:29.478 --> 00:22:31.915
Yeah, I had to meet a guy out
on Old Sheltham Road

342
00:22:31.959 --> 00:22:35.092
to talk about some damage that
the storm did to his place.

343
00:22:35.136 --> 00:22:37.834
Is the guy
at the Old Sheltham Road

344
00:22:37.878 --> 00:22:40.968
the only one who knows that you
were going there?

345
00:22:41.011 --> 00:22:42.535
He cut off my finger.

346
00:22:42.578 --> 00:22:44.014
Did you stop and
get gas first?

347
00:22:44.058 --> 00:22:45.494
The finger that I
was born with.

348
00:22:45.538 --> 00:22:47.191
The finger I had from
my whole life.

349
00:22:47.235 --> 00:22:48.802
That my mother gave me.

350
00:22:48.845 --> 00:22:50.194
Was the drive-through one of
those restaurants you can see

351
00:22:50.238 --> 00:22:51.674
from the highway?

352
00:22:51.718 --> 00:22:52.675
And we're talking about
fucking hamburgers?!

353
00:22:52.719 --> 00:22:53.676
You need to focus--

354
00:22:53.720 --> 00:22:58.725
[timer alarm]

355
00:23:03.556 --> 00:23:07.908
[door rattling]

356
00:23:15.698 --> 00:23:17.265
Hero: What did
you figure out?

357
00:23:17.308 --> 00:23:18.875
We figured out that you're
a fuckin' homo.

358
00:23:18.919 --> 00:23:19.876
Oliver: Ron!

359
00:23:19.920 --> 00:23:21.748
The answer is obvious.

360
00:23:21.791 --> 00:23:24.664
Other than the fact that in the two newspapers you gave us

361
00:23:24.707 --> 00:23:27.449
we had one article
in common.

362
00:23:27.493 --> 00:23:29.320
There is no connection
whatsoever

363
00:23:29.364 --> 00:23:31.410
between the
two of us.

364
00:23:31.453 --> 00:23:33.716
Clearly there's a purpose
behind my presence.

365
00:23:33.760 --> 00:23:36.763
Everything about my
abduction was planned.

366
00:23:36.806 --> 00:23:38.721
It required prior
knowledge.

367
00:23:38.765 --> 00:23:40.549
On the other hand,

368
00:23:40.593 --> 00:23:43.552
Ron's abductions appears to
be completely at random.

369
00:23:43.596 --> 00:23:45.336
No one, not even Ron
would've known

370
00:23:45.380 --> 00:23:47.164
where he was
going to be then.

371
00:23:47.208 --> 00:23:49.166
So I believe that he
was picked up

372
00:23:49.210 --> 00:23:51.473
simply because he was
visible from the highway.

373
00:23:51.517 --> 00:23:53.736
Yeah, so what the fuck
am I doing here?

374
00:23:53.780 --> 00:23:58.741
To prove the depths he's willing
to go to in dealing with me.

375
00:23:58.785 --> 00:24:02.179
Hero: We've got a problem
in our society.

376
00:24:02.223 --> 00:24:05.444
Nothing that we say has
any value anymore.

377
00:24:05.487 --> 00:24:07.141
No credibility.

378
00:24:07.184 --> 00:24:09.099
I say I'm gonna pay my
bills it doesn't matter.

379
00:24:09.143 --> 00:24:11.885
The lender needs a credit
check to prove that I have.

380
00:24:11.928 --> 00:24:13.147
To prove that
I will--

381
00:24:13.190 --> 00:24:16.803
I'll give you $22,500
to let me go.

382
00:24:18.152 --> 00:24:19.762
Nobody believes anything
we say anymore

383
00:24:19.806 --> 00:24:21.329
without proof
of intention.

384
00:24:21.372 --> 00:24:24.288
So if I say that I'm gonna kill
a man I need to prove

385
00:24:24.332 --> 00:24:28.292
that I have
killed a man.

386
00:24:28.336 --> 00:24:31.861
Proof of intention.

387
00:24:31.905 --> 00:24:33.080
You need to
stop now.

388
00:24:33.123 --> 00:24:34.516
I really can't
do that.

389
00:24:34.560 --> 00:24:36.518
Oliver: I will take you
at your word.

390
00:24:36.562 --> 00:24:37.780
That should be
good enough.

391
00:24:37.824 --> 00:24:39.782
With that assurance,

392
00:24:39.826 --> 00:24:44.308
any other proof of your
sincerity is not necessary.

393
00:24:44.352 --> 00:24:45.832
That's true.

394
00:24:45.875 --> 00:24:48.399
Except it's not you I
have to convince.

395
00:24:48.443 --> 00:24:49.792
It's them.

396
00:24:49.836 --> 00:24:59.846
♪

397
00:25:01.325 --> 00:25:06.330
[indistinct chatter]

398
00:25:13.337 --> 00:25:17.298
[phones ringing]

399
00:25:23.696 --> 00:25:25.828
I heard they gave you
the shift today.

400
00:25:25.872 --> 00:25:27.569
I thought it
was a joke.

401
00:25:27.613 --> 00:25:29.136
On me.

402
00:25:29.179 --> 00:25:30.572
Or probably
because everyone

403
00:25:30.616 --> 00:25:32.792
is still too drunk
from the party.

404
00:25:32.835 --> 00:25:35.185
How much damage could a
retiring desk jockey do

405
00:25:35.229 --> 00:25:37.144
on a Saturday,
anyway?

406
00:25:38.319 --> 00:25:41.757
Lt. Roy! You got an incoming!

407
00:25:41.801 --> 00:25:43.498
They're not wasting
any time.

408
00:25:43.542 --> 00:25:45.761
Well the plan is the whole
building be empty by Friday.

409
00:25:45.805 --> 00:25:47.589
The new HQ is already
fully operational.

410
00:25:47.633 --> 00:25:49.112
They asked for
the duty officer?

411
00:25:49.156 --> 00:25:51.506
Nope. You. By name.

412
00:25:52.638 --> 00:25:53.987
Darnley?

413
00:25:54.030 --> 00:25:55.728
Didn't we have an
agreement last year?

414
00:25:55.771 --> 00:25:58.165
No more hacking city computer
systems. Parking--

415
00:25:58.208 --> 00:25:59.645
Yeah.This is different.

416
00:25:59.688 --> 00:26:01.124
What have you
done now?

417
00:26:01.168 --> 00:26:03.387
I'm sending you a link.
Go there. Now.

418
00:26:03.431 --> 00:26:05.389
One of my chat groups
sent me this.

419
00:26:05.433 --> 00:26:07.609
You ever hear of a place
called Zoop's Chicken?

420
00:26:07.653 --> 00:26:09.350
It's up highway nine.

421
00:26:09.393 --> 00:26:12.135
That means whatever
this is it might be local.

422
00:26:15.051 --> 00:26:16.531
You got it? You seeing this?

423
00:26:16.575 --> 00:26:18.054
What am I
looking at?

424
00:26:18.098 --> 00:26:20.100
This is live and I'm
pretty sure it's real.

425
00:26:20.143 --> 00:26:22.493
You don't want to do this.
It is unnecessary.

426
00:26:22.537 --> 00:26:23.973
It's not a question
of want.

427
00:26:24.017 --> 00:26:25.627
It's a question
of need.

428
00:26:25.671 --> 00:26:28.064
We need to give gravitas
to the procedure to come.

429
00:26:28.108 --> 00:26:29.849
Oliver: What procedure?

430
00:26:29.892 --> 00:26:38.553
♪

431
00:26:38.597 --> 00:26:42.209
[phone vibrates]

432
00:26:42.252 --> 00:26:44.037
[phone vibrates]

433
00:26:45.038 --> 00:26:46.648
Shit!

434
00:26:46.692 --> 00:26:49.869
Hey, it's that
creepy guy.

435
00:26:49.912 --> 00:26:51.914
Slosson's not gonna give
me the interview.

436
00:26:51.958 --> 00:26:54.003
He's going to CBS.

437
00:26:54.047 --> 00:26:55.570
A Congressman from
Ass Grease, West Virginia,

438
00:26:55.614 --> 00:26:58.442
and he's lied
to me.

439
00:26:58.486 --> 00:27:00.662
The world is nothin' but
creepy guys, Kaitlyn. Which one?

440
00:27:00.706 --> 00:27:02.098
At 53 Division.

441
00:27:02.142 --> 00:27:03.796
His name is Eddie.

442
00:27:03.839 --> 00:27:06.712
And yes he's very creepy, but
creepy's how we get things done.

443
00:27:06.755 --> 00:27:08.191
He's devoted to me.

444
00:27:08.235 --> 00:27:10.237
Okay, well he just said
if you don't want it,

445
00:27:10.280 --> 00:27:12.718
he's gonna give it to Channel
6 in four minutes.

446
00:27:12.761 --> 00:27:14.850
Cocksucker!

447
00:27:14.894 --> 00:27:16.286
Thank you.

448
00:27:20.726 --> 00:27:21.944
[message alert]

449
00:27:25.339 --> 00:27:26.819
You know this
is too much.

450
00:27:26.862 --> 00:27:28.429
Hero: How do
you figure?

451
00:27:28.472 --> 00:27:30.170
If we're really being honest
with each other,

452
00:27:30.213 --> 00:27:31.737
and pretty soon we're
gonna have

453
00:27:31.780 --> 00:27:33.564
to be very honest
with each other.

454
00:27:33.608 --> 00:27:37.481
We both know that this
is absolutely necessary.

455
00:27:37.525 --> 00:27:38.831
This will keep it real.

456
00:27:38.874 --> 00:27:40.615
This will keep
their attention.

457
00:27:40.659 --> 00:27:43.705
You don't think cutting off
his finger was real enough?

458
00:27:43.749 --> 00:27:44.706
Live?

459
00:27:44.750 --> 00:27:45.751
Well, it looks live.

460
00:27:45.794 --> 00:27:47.143
We can't really tell.

461
00:27:48.667 --> 00:27:51.147
You're not in charge.

462
00:27:51.191 --> 00:27:52.627
Not in this room.

463
00:27:53.672 --> 00:27:54.716
What do you mean?

464
00:27:54.760 --> 00:27:55.978
This room?

465
00:28:19.045 --> 00:28:20.307
I'm sorry.

466
00:28:20.350 --> 00:28:23.702
[whimpering]

467
00:28:34.887 --> 00:28:36.758
What is this about?

468
00:28:36.802 --> 00:28:38.325
Really?

469
00:28:41.589 --> 00:28:43.634
Justice.

470
00:28:43.678 --> 00:28:47.421
[whimpering]

471
00:28:50.337 --> 00:28:51.555
[gun shot]

472
00:28:51.599 --> 00:28:53.035
[gasps]

473
00:28:55.385 --> 00:28:57.561
Holy shit.

474
00:28:57.605 --> 00:28:59.215
Sweet Jesus!

475
00:29:03.219 --> 00:29:05.178
Do I have your
attention now?

476
00:29:14.361 --> 00:29:19.366
[panicked chatter]

477
00:29:20.628 --> 00:29:21.672
That was live.

478
00:29:21.716 --> 00:29:22.673
No, we can't
verify that.

479
00:29:22.717 --> 00:29:23.674
It looked live!

480
00:29:23.718 --> 00:29:25.154
Yes, everything
looks live.

481
00:29:32.814 --> 00:29:37.776
[grunting]

482
00:29:40.822 --> 00:29:48.830
♪

483
00:30:10.112 --> 00:30:13.246
We need anyone we can get from
tech support down here now.

484
00:30:13.289 --> 00:30:15.596
Yes I'll hold.

485
00:30:15.639 --> 00:30:19.078
Sir, shouldn't we get
Lt. Lucas, sir? Someone--

486
00:30:19.121 --> 00:30:22.124
With more field
experience?

487
00:30:22.168 --> 00:30:24.300
Certainly should.

488
00:30:24.344 --> 00:30:27.129
I don't think we're gonna
have enough time.

489
00:30:51.501 --> 00:30:56.463
Well...Now that that's done,
what should happen now?

490
00:30:56.506 --> 00:30:58.900
I don't understand.

491
00:30:58.944 --> 00:31:00.423
What should happen
to me?

492
00:31:00.467 --> 00:31:03.731
What does the State
say should be done?

493
00:31:03.774 --> 00:31:06.647
I don't think I'm qualified to
say what should be done

494
00:31:06.690 --> 00:31:07.909
or what shouldn't
be done.

495
00:31:07.953 --> 00:31:09.868
Of course you're qualified.

496
00:31:09.911 --> 00:31:11.739
I beg your pardon?

497
00:31:11.782 --> 00:31:14.220
You already said that you
were in the legal profession.

498
00:31:14.263 --> 00:31:16.962
At the very least, someone in the legal profession would know

499
00:31:17.005 --> 00:31:18.485
the laws of their
own state.

500
00:31:18.528 --> 00:31:20.574
I see what
you're saying.

501
00:31:20.617 --> 00:31:23.751
Uh...Well then you
should be arrested,

502
00:31:23.794 --> 00:31:28.756
incarcerated, indicted,
and tried.

503
00:31:28.799 --> 00:31:30.236
And?

504
00:31:30.279 --> 00:31:32.020
If you were to be
found guilty--

505
00:31:32.064 --> 00:31:34.022
If? If I was to be
found guilty?

506
00:31:34.066 --> 00:31:36.329
You were right here.
You saw the whole thing.

507
00:31:36.372 --> 00:31:38.331
All these cameras were
here to secure witness.

508
00:31:38.374 --> 00:31:41.160
If the jury were to
find you guilty

509
00:31:41.203 --> 00:31:44.554
and recommend the
maximum sentence...

510
00:31:44.598 --> 00:31:47.296
Well, in this state you
would be condemned

511
00:31:47.340 --> 00:31:48.558
to pay the ultimate
price--

512
00:31:48.602 --> 00:31:49.820
And what would
that be?

513
00:31:49.864 --> 00:31:51.300
You would pay
with your life.

514
00:31:51.344 --> 00:31:52.823
You would be
put to death.

515
00:31:52.867 --> 00:31:55.174
Like the guy in
the paper.

516
00:31:55.217 --> 00:31:57.437
Yes if you were convicted
of a capital crime,

517
00:31:57.480 --> 00:31:58.960
but you may
not be.

518
00:31:59.004 --> 00:32:00.788
No two cases
are the same.

519
00:32:00.831 --> 00:32:02.964
But the punishment is the same
regardless of the case,

520
00:32:03.008 --> 00:32:05.401
because an innocent
person was killed.

521
00:32:05.445 --> 00:32:07.664
Cut and dry. Seems to me
that's the idea.

522
00:32:07.708 --> 00:32:09.710
I don't quite understand
what you're getting at.

523
00:32:09.753 --> 00:32:11.973
I picked a man up,
I brought him here,

524
00:32:12.017 --> 00:32:13.975
I tied him up,
and I killed him.

525
00:32:14.019 --> 00:32:16.543
As far as we know he was
an innocent man

526
00:32:16.586 --> 00:32:18.023
who never did anything
to anybody.

527
00:32:18.066 --> 00:32:19.807
So there's no two
ways about it.

528
00:32:19.850 --> 00:32:22.114
We're talking about
the death penalty.

529
00:32:22.157 --> 00:32:24.855
Right here. Both papers.

530
00:32:24.899 --> 00:32:26.379
Big story.

531
00:32:29.382 --> 00:32:31.166
The Jeeter case?

532
00:32:31.210 --> 00:32:33.342
The Jeeter case. Read it.

533
00:32:33.386 --> 00:32:34.387
Out loud to everyone.

534
00:32:34.430 --> 00:32:35.954
The whole thing.

535
00:32:37.172 --> 00:32:41.176
[paper rustling]

536
00:32:44.049 --> 00:32:47.966
"Paul William Gager, the
man who abducted

537
00:32:48.009 --> 00:32:52.579
and murdered 14 year old
Claudine Jeeter six years ago,

538
00:32:52.622 --> 00:32:55.843
was put to death this
morning at 12:01.

539
00:32:55.886 --> 00:32:58.324
Death was administered
by lethal injection

540
00:32:58.367 --> 00:33:02.893
at the Six Rivers Correctional
Facility in Triborough.

541
00:33:02.937 --> 00:33:05.984
It was the swiftest enforcement
of the death penalty

542
00:33:06.027 --> 00:33:08.769
in the state's history."

543
00:33:10.945 --> 00:33:12.425
Well, I suspect there's
significantly more

544
00:33:12.468 --> 00:33:15.384
to the story
than that.

545
00:33:15.428 --> 00:33:17.430
Um..."A last minute
appeal

546
00:33:17.473 --> 00:33:20.868
by Gager's lawyers
was unsuccessful.

547
00:33:20.911 --> 00:33:23.958
Gager was convicted
of Jeeter's abduction

548
00:33:24.002 --> 00:33:28.049
and murder after a
two-year manhunt.

549
00:33:28.093 --> 00:33:30.791
Jeeter went missing
from her house

550
00:33:30.834 --> 00:33:33.620
on February the 10th,
six years ago."

551
00:33:36.623 --> 00:33:37.972
I'm not bored.

552
00:33:40.018 --> 00:33:43.369
"It was discovered later that
Claudine had been held

553
00:33:43.412 --> 00:33:47.373
in a home-made facility
for keeping rabbits

554
00:33:47.416 --> 00:33:51.594
on Gager's property, three
miles from the Jeeter house.

555
00:33:51.638 --> 00:33:55.555
The search for Claudine Jeeter
was exhaustive and emotional--

556
00:33:55.598 --> 00:33:57.339
I know him.

557
00:33:57.383 --> 00:33:59.124
--and gained a great deal of
public attention as local

558
00:33:59.167 --> 00:34:00.255
and state police--

559
00:34:00.299 --> 00:34:01.648
We all know him,
don't we?

560
00:34:01.691 --> 00:34:03.171
--followed lead
after lead..."

561
00:34:03.215 --> 00:34:06.566
"...Until finally they were able
to apprehend Gager

562
00:34:06.609 --> 00:34:09.177
and link him to
the girl's death."

563
00:34:11.136 --> 00:34:14.922
Um...That's
all there is.

564
00:34:14.965 --> 00:34:16.880
There isn't anymore.

565
00:34:21.059 --> 00:34:24.366
Maybe not in the paper, but
in fact there's a lot more.

566
00:34:24.410 --> 00:34:26.629
But I wanna make sure
I've got this right,

567
00:34:26.673 --> 00:34:28.936
so if the court was right
in that sentence,

568
00:34:28.979 --> 00:34:31.460
and the state was
right in exacting

569
00:34:31.504 --> 00:34:33.375
the ultimate punishment,
then it follows --

570
00:34:33.419 --> 00:34:34.942
as I have clearly
stated --

571
00:34:34.985 --> 00:34:36.509
that I should
be executed

572
00:34:36.552 --> 00:34:38.163
for killing our dear friend
Ron resting outside.

573
00:34:38.206 --> 00:34:39.947
No, you cannot say
that for sure.

574
00:34:39.990 --> 00:34:41.949
I picked a man up
off the street,

575
00:34:41.992 --> 00:34:44.473
I abducted him, I took
him out of his life.

576
00:34:44.517 --> 00:34:45.953
But there are
other issues.

577
00:34:45.996 --> 00:34:47.781
The mental state of the
accused, the IQ--

578
00:34:47.824 --> 00:34:49.826
I brought him here,
I tied him up,

579
00:34:49.870 --> 00:34:52.960
and I tortured him, and I killed
him for my own reasons.

580
00:34:53.003 --> 00:34:54.440
What's not for
sure about that?

581
00:34:54.483 --> 00:34:56.181
You'll need a trial
to determine that.

582
00:34:56.224 --> 00:34:57.791
Why?

583
00:34:57.834 --> 00:34:59.575
Because without a trial
there can be no justice.

584
00:34:59.619 --> 00:35:02.056
Well that's an area you would
know quite a lot about,

585
00:35:02.100 --> 00:35:03.797
wouldn't you?

586
00:35:03.840 --> 00:35:05.668
...Your Honour.

587
00:35:12.066 --> 00:35:16.070
[typing]

588
00:35:16.114 --> 00:35:24.774
♪

589
00:35:24.818 --> 00:35:26.167
Judge Oliver Straight.

590
00:35:26.211 --> 00:35:28.691
The man who tried
the Jeeter case.

591
00:35:28.735 --> 00:35:31.607
Hero: A man is guilty for taking the life of another man.

592
00:35:31.651 --> 00:35:34.132
If convicted, that guilty man
must be put to death.

593
00:35:34.175 --> 00:35:36.134
These are the rules we've
established, yes?

594
00:35:36.177 --> 00:35:37.918
Don't say yes.

595
00:35:39.485 --> 00:35:44.185
In this state, yes.

596
00:35:44.229 --> 00:35:47.188
That "yes" means that we can
be a little bit more focused,

597
00:35:47.232 --> 00:35:48.624
doesn't it?

598
00:35:48.668 --> 00:35:50.670
I have Carl on the
phone for you.

599
00:35:50.713 --> 00:35:53.194
Tell Carl we need to control
the cutting ourselves.

600
00:35:53.238 --> 00:35:56.154
Yeah, well he's not so crazy
about going live at all.

601
00:35:56.197 --> 00:35:57.198
That's true to form.

602
00:35:57.242 --> 00:35:59.853
Which is why we're
number four.

603
00:35:59.896 --> 00:36:01.463
Carl.

604
00:36:01.507 --> 00:36:04.292
I put it to you, Judge,
that if that is the case,

605
00:36:04.336 --> 00:36:06.120
things don't look
too good for you.

606
00:36:06.164 --> 00:36:08.253
Because surely as I shot
poor innocent Ron,

607
00:36:08.296 --> 00:36:10.646
you're also guilty of taking
an innocent man's life.

608
00:36:10.690 --> 00:36:11.908
What man would
that be?

609
00:36:11.952 --> 00:36:13.214
You just read
the article.

610
00:36:13.258 --> 00:36:14.824
The Jeeter case.
Paul William Gager.

611
00:36:14.868 --> 00:36:17.305
I can prove that you willingly
and knowingly put him,

612
00:36:17.349 --> 00:36:18.959
an innocent man
to death.

613
00:36:19.002 --> 00:36:20.874
And I'm ready to try that
case right here.

614
00:36:20.917 --> 00:36:22.876
Right now in front of this
particular judge.

615
00:36:22.919 --> 00:36:24.704
And in front of this
particular jury.

616
00:36:24.747 --> 00:36:26.227
I don't understand.

617
00:36:26.271 --> 00:36:27.620
Yes you do.

618
00:36:27.663 --> 00:36:28.795
They're right here.
They're everywhere.

619
00:36:28.838 --> 00:36:30.362
And I assure
you, Judge,

620
00:36:30.405 --> 00:36:32.842
these wheels of justice
will turn very quickly.

621
00:36:34.844 --> 00:36:36.759
Now Carl! Now!

622
00:36:36.803 --> 00:36:38.239
Because they will beat
us, that's why!

623
00:36:38.283 --> 00:36:40.633
We are not supposed
to be beaten!

624
00:36:42.809 --> 00:36:45.507
For those joining
us late--

625
00:36:45.551 --> 00:36:47.074
--I'm going to conduct a trial
for the life of the Judge.

626
00:36:47.117 --> 00:36:49.207
And whatever you decide,
I will abide by,

627
00:36:49.250 --> 00:36:50.730
but let's be
perfectly clear.

628
00:36:50.773 --> 00:36:52.427
We're going by the
rules of the state.

629
00:36:52.471 --> 00:36:54.299
The Judge's rules.

630
00:36:54.342 --> 00:36:57.258
That means on a verdict of guilty he will be put to death.

631
00:36:57.302 --> 00:36:59.217
Right here.

632
00:37:04.874 --> 00:37:07.007
Court is in
session.

633
00:37:07.050 --> 00:37:12.055
[indistinct chatter]

634
00:37:18.714 --> 00:37:20.194
Isolate and find!

635
00:37:20.238 --> 00:37:21.978
Let's get on to what we
know about Straight,

636
00:37:22.022 --> 00:37:24.024
not what we
think we know.

637
00:37:24.067 --> 00:37:26.940
[news bulletin music]

638
00:37:26.983 --> 00:37:28.333
Good afternoon.

639
00:37:28.376 --> 00:37:30.248
Harper Grant with a
special USCN report.

640
00:37:30.291 --> 00:37:31.466
Here's what we know.

641
00:37:31.510 --> 00:37:33.294
God help us.

642
00:37:33.338 --> 00:37:34.295
The judge who tried the
Claudine Jeeter abduction

643
00:37:34.339 --> 00:37:35.644
and murder trial,

644
00:37:35.688 --> 00:37:37.559
has himself apparently
been abducted

645
00:37:37.603 --> 00:37:39.996
and is now being held at an
undisclosed location.

646
00:37:40.040 --> 00:37:41.476
The abduction, however,

647
00:37:41.520 --> 00:37:43.522
