coming home to roost?

654
00:37:56.491 --> 00:37:58.493
Jean: You can look
at it that way.

655
00:37:58.537 --> 00:38:00.016
Did you ever hear
anyone question

656
00:38:00.060 --> 00:38:02.323
how Judge Straight
handled the case?

657
00:38:02.367 --> 00:38:03.846
They will now.

658
00:38:03.890 --> 00:38:06.675
At the least we know that
a member of the public

659
00:38:06.719 --> 00:38:08.764
has decided to
question the trial.

660
00:38:08.808 --> 00:38:13.073
Harper: And perhaps even
that verdict is in question.

661
00:38:13.116 --> 00:38:16.119
Now Darnley made references to
credit checks and overdue bills.

662
00:38:16.163 --> 00:38:17.860
There could be
something there.

663
00:38:17.904 --> 00:38:19.993
Where are they pulling
this stuff from?

664
00:38:21.908 --> 00:38:22.909
Who's this?

665
00:38:22.952 --> 00:38:24.084
It's the IT team.

666
00:38:24.127 --> 00:38:25.259
You're kidding.

667
00:38:25.303 --> 00:38:26.260
They're all in the
new building.

668
00:38:26.304 --> 00:38:27.914
What can you
tell me?

669
00:38:27.957 --> 00:38:29.394
We can't trace a stream to
a social media interface.

670
00:38:29.437 --> 00:38:30.960
Why not?

671
00:38:31.004 --> 00:38:33.615
Isn't he using their server
or whatever it is?

672
00:38:33.659 --> 00:38:36.444
Think of it as telephone that's
been redirected fifteen times.

673
00:38:36.488 --> 00:38:38.054
So he's smart in
that way?

674
00:38:38.098 --> 00:38:39.142
Pretty much.

675
00:38:39.186 --> 00:38:40.709
Can't they
take him off?

676
00:38:40.753 --> 00:38:42.624
They could of course shut
the whole thing down,

677
00:38:42.668 --> 00:38:45.410
but then there's nothing to say
he couldn't just show up

678
00:38:45.453 --> 00:38:46.585
on any other
platform.

679
00:38:46.628 --> 00:38:48.456
Yeah, it's a bad
idea anyway.

680
00:38:48.500 --> 00:38:51.764
And we would lose our only means
of knowing what he's up to.

681
00:38:51.807 --> 00:38:53.243
[phone ringing]

682
00:38:53.287 --> 00:38:55.811
Can we limit the reach
or whatever you call it.

683
00:38:55.855 --> 00:38:56.986
Possibly.

684
00:38:57.030 --> 00:38:57.987
Will he know if
we do that?

685
00:38:58.031 --> 00:38:59.249
Almost certainly.

686
00:38:59.293 --> 00:39:00.250
How can you
be so sure?

687
00:39:00.294 --> 00:39:01.904
He broke into

688
00:39:01.948 --> 00:39:03.253
one of the world's
most controlled websites,

689
00:39:03.297 --> 00:39:04.516
bootlegged a live signal
without a trace

690
00:39:04.559 --> 00:39:06.082
and scrambled it a
half dozen times --

691
00:39:06.126 --> 00:39:08.128
my guess is he's smart
enough to track

692
00:39:08.171 --> 00:39:09.608
what's happening
on his own site.

693
00:39:09.651 --> 00:39:11.827
Okay. Thank you.

694
00:39:11.871 --> 00:39:13.873
Okay, so the Judge
lives in Aspian County.

695
00:39:13.916 --> 00:39:15.135
20 miles outside
city centre.

696
00:39:15.178 --> 00:39:16.615
We have two
cruisers there now.

697
00:39:16.658 --> 00:39:18.312
They found an open
Volvo wagon

698
00:39:18.356 --> 00:39:20.923
and a whole mess of groceries
spilled out onto the driveway.

699
00:39:20.967 --> 00:39:22.664
But we don't know
when it happened.

700
00:39:22.708 --> 00:39:24.013
So we're running
a check

701
00:39:24.057 --> 00:39:25.711
on all surveillance cameras
and any of the--

702
00:39:25.754 --> 00:39:26.712
Check the cash
register tape.

703
00:39:26.755 --> 00:39:28.017
What?

704
00:39:28.061 --> 00:39:29.541
In one of the bags
on the driveway.

705
00:39:29.584 --> 00:39:32.239
It'll tell us the store and
the time of purchase.

706
00:39:32.282 --> 00:39:34.807
If no tape, check the bags
or the price stickers

707
00:39:34.850 --> 00:39:37.592
to figure out which store,
go to the nearest one,

708
00:39:37.636 --> 00:39:40.116
and get the time of purchase
from the manager.

709
00:39:40.160 --> 00:39:45.034
The receipt will give us
where the Judge is.

710
00:39:45.078 --> 00:39:47.428
If the Judge bought his
groceries at 10 a.m.

711
00:39:47.472 --> 00:39:49.299
and this thing
went live at --

712
00:39:49.343 --> 00:39:51.084
1:11.

713
00:39:51.127 --> 00:39:53.608
1:11, and a man can only drive
sixty five miles an hour

714
00:39:53.652 --> 00:39:56.176
without attracting attention,
then the room they're in

715
00:39:56.219 --> 00:40:00.398
is no more than a hundred mile
radius from the Judge's house.

716
00:40:00.441 --> 00:40:05.403
Now if we allow for fixing
up the room and picking up

717
00:40:05.446 --> 00:40:08.928
the other abductee, it's
probably even closer.

718
00:40:08.971 --> 00:40:10.930
What have you got
on the other one?

719
00:40:10.973 --> 00:40:13.193
We went back to the start
of the transmission

720
00:40:13.236 --> 00:40:15.456
and we figured out
it's a local. Ron Price.

721
00:40:15.500 --> 00:40:17.240
He owns and operates
Priced to Pleaze--

722
00:40:17.284 --> 00:40:18.677
that's spelt
with a "Z".

723
00:40:18.720 --> 00:40:20.940
Now he has an ex-wife
who's still his dispatcher.

724
00:40:20.983 --> 00:40:22.028
She said
his first job this morning

725
00:40:22.071 --> 00:40:24.726
was out near Sheltenham.

726
00:40:24.770 --> 00:40:29.731
So if our man picked up
Mr. Price after the judge,

727
00:40:29.775 --> 00:40:33.474
that means our location
is very local.

728
00:40:33.518 --> 00:40:36.434
Well it's patently clear
that you have thought

729
00:40:36.477 --> 00:40:40.525
this through thoroughly,
and intelligently--

730
00:40:40.568 --> 00:40:42.309
Don't condescend to me.

731
00:40:44.964 --> 00:40:49.925
--But you have made some
fundamental errors

732
00:40:49.969 --> 00:40:54.452
when it comes to
judicial process.

733
00:40:54.495 --> 00:40:58.412
You say you're going
to conduct a trial.

734
00:40:58.456 --> 00:41:00.240
You can't.

735
00:41:00.283 --> 00:41:01.763
A trial, a trial--

736
00:41:01.807 --> 00:41:03.852
"Is the examination of
evidence and applicable law

737
00:41:03.896 --> 00:41:05.506
by a competent tribunal
to determine

738
00:41:05.550 --> 00:41:08.335
the specific issues of
charges and claims."

739
00:41:08.378 --> 00:41:10.598
All right. All right. All right.

740
00:41:10.642 --> 00:41:15.298
Let's look at "applicable law
in a competent tribunal--"

741
00:41:15.342 --> 00:41:16.909
But we don't
have to.

742
00:41:16.952 --> 00:41:19.433
Because we already know
what law we're talking about.

743
00:41:19.477 --> 00:41:20.739
Premeditated murder.

744
00:41:20.782 --> 00:41:22.436
And as far as a competent
tribunal goes,

745
00:41:22.480 --> 00:41:24.090
well, I'm just
picking my jury

746
00:41:24.133 --> 00:41:26.353
from the same pot you
chose yours from.

747
00:41:26.396 --> 00:41:28.094
All that informs a
trial are rules.

748
00:41:28.137 --> 00:41:30.139
We'll have those.
And we'll have temperance.

749
00:41:30.183 --> 00:41:31.750
That makes
this a trial.

750
00:41:31.793 --> 00:41:33.578
But we'll have something your
courtroom doesn't have,

751
00:41:33.621 --> 00:41:35.318
or doesn't have
very often.

752
00:41:35.362 --> 00:41:37.625
Which is?

753
00:41:37.669 --> 00:41:39.758
Justice.

754
00:41:39.801 --> 00:41:42.543
I will be the prosecutor and
you will be defending yourself.

755
00:41:42.587 --> 00:41:44.589
Out there will be the
judge and jury.

756
00:41:44.632 --> 00:41:46.112
The Judge speaks
in a trial.

757
00:41:46.155 --> 00:41:49.376
This Judge will speak.

758
00:41:54.468 --> 00:41:56.209
Terry: Holy Shit.

759
00:42:01.431 --> 00:42:02.955
From the moment Claudine
Jeeter was taken

760
00:42:02.998 --> 00:42:04.565
she was front
page news.

761
00:42:04.609 --> 00:42:06.567
A fourteen year old girl,
straight A student,

762
00:42:06.611 --> 00:42:08.351
with a little pet terrier
named Brownie--

763
00:42:08.395 --> 00:42:10.571
plucked out of her world on
her way home from school.

764
00:42:10.615 --> 00:42:12.355
Everyone was gripped.

765
00:42:12.399 --> 00:42:15.184
The public, the police,
the Judge to be. Everyone.

766
00:42:15.228 --> 00:42:16.969
We all saw the Grandmother
Mrs. Solsza

767
00:42:17.012 --> 00:42:20.233
on our TV's practically every
night, as well as the cousin,

768
00:42:20.276 --> 00:42:22.540
the family spokesman,
Bertinad Solsza.

769
00:42:22.583 --> 00:42:24.367
They became fixtures
in our living room,

770
00:42:24.411 --> 00:42:26.108
part of our
news, reality.

771
00:42:26.152 --> 00:42:28.197
As a result, the prosecution
will argue that the verdict

772
00:42:28.241 --> 00:42:30.069
in the Jeeter case was
manufactured instead

773
00:42:30.112 --> 00:42:31.636
of arrived at in
the courtroom.

774
00:42:31.679 --> 00:42:33.246
Not out of malice,

775
00:42:33.289 --> 00:42:34.987
but out of genuinely honest
outrage and desire.

776
00:42:35.030 --> 00:42:38.686
A desire to see someone pay for
the killing of young Claudine.

777
00:42:38.730 --> 00:42:41.733
But the prosecution will prove
that as a result of this desire

778
00:42:41.776 --> 00:42:43.517
there was a race to
the gallows.

779
00:42:43.561 --> 00:42:45.737
A race run on the fuel of
police incompetence

780
00:42:45.780 --> 00:42:47.390
and judicial corner-cutting,

781
00:42:47.434 --> 00:42:50.219
civil servants recreant
to their duty

782
00:42:50.263 --> 00:42:52.308
so an innocent man
was put to death.

783
00:42:52.352 --> 00:42:54.572
Whether the state thought Paul
William Gager was guilty

784
00:42:54.615 --> 00:42:56.182
or not is not
the point.

785
00:42:56.225 --> 00:42:58.358
Does it matter if I thought
Ron the roofer

786
00:42:58.401 --> 00:43:00.142
was guilty of some
crime only later

787
00:43:00.186 --> 00:43:02.144
to discover that he wasn't?
Of course not.

788
00:43:02.188 --> 00:43:04.364
All that matters
is I killed him

789
00:43:04.407 --> 00:43:06.018
and I had no right to kill him.

790
00:43:06.061 --> 00:43:07.672
The state killed Paul
William Gager

791
00:43:07.715 --> 00:43:09.674
and they had no
right to kill him.

792
00:43:09.717 --> 00:43:12.459
The prosecution will prove this beyond the shadow of a doubt

793
00:43:12.502 --> 00:43:14.940
by pointing out that his arrest
and trial was systematic

794
00:43:14.983 --> 00:43:18.334
of a justice system that
is ignorant, corrupt,

795
00:43:18.378 --> 00:43:20.075
and bloodthirsty.

796
00:43:23.949 --> 00:43:25.994
This is not how
it's done.

797
00:43:27.256 --> 00:43:28.736
Are you speaking
as the defense?

798
00:43:28.780 --> 00:43:30.477
No.

799
00:43:30.520 --> 00:43:32.174
Well you can only speak if
you're speaking as the defense.

800
00:43:32.218 --> 00:43:34.742
I can only speak as myself, I
can't speak as the defense.

801
00:43:34.786 --> 00:43:36.614
Then you don't have a
voice, unless it's as

802
00:43:36.657 --> 00:43:38.267
the defense addressing
the court.

803
00:43:38.311 --> 00:43:42.707
Because, as I have already
said, this is not a court.

804
00:43:42.750 --> 00:43:47.189
Believe me when I say you
can make a great study

805
00:43:47.233 --> 00:43:52.194
of a dictionary and brilliantly
mimic the way lawyers speak,

806
00:43:52.238 --> 00:43:55.415
but that does not mean
you understand the law.

807
00:43:55.458 --> 00:43:57.591
You're saying I don't
understand the law?

808
00:43:57.635 --> 00:44:00.942
I am saying you do
not understand the law.

809
00:44:00.986 --> 00:44:02.422
Exhibit A for the
prosecution!

810
00:44:02.465 --> 00:44:03.771
The Judge's error.

811
00:44:03.815 --> 00:44:05.120
Assumptions
without reference.

812
00:44:05.164 --> 00:44:06.774
Judgements without support.

813
00:44:06.818 --> 00:44:09.037
The modus operandi of the
man in the black robe

814
00:44:09.081 --> 00:44:10.430
to make snap
judgements.

815
00:44:10.473 --> 00:44:12.171
This is not my
kind of law.

816
00:44:12.214 --> 00:44:13.955
Yes this is your
kind of law.

817
00:44:13.999 --> 00:44:15.957
And this is not my
kind of courtroom.

818
00:44:16.001 --> 00:44:18.177
Yes, this is your
kind of courtroom.

819
00:44:18.220 --> 00:44:20.788
The Jeeter case
was a capital case.

820
00:44:20.832 --> 00:44:23.269
There is a
judge, yes.

821
00:44:23.312 --> 00:44:26.141
But the verdict is reached
at by the jury,

822
00:44:26.185 --> 00:44:28.317
and they recommend
the sentence.

823
00:44:28.361 --> 00:44:32.191
The role of the magistrate
is considerably limited.

824
00:44:32.234 --> 00:44:35.716
I expect you
know that.

825
00:44:35.760 --> 00:44:40.634
But there is something else
going on here that concerns me.

826
00:44:40.678 --> 00:44:42.201
Ah.

827
00:44:42.244 --> 00:44:45.639
No doubt you'll let
us all know.

828
00:44:45.683 --> 00:44:49.121
I don't believe you have
the right to try this case.

829
00:44:49.164 --> 00:44:52.515
Not under any
circumstances.

830
00:44:52.559 --> 00:44:54.474
Is anybody here
a lawyer?

831
00:44:55.780 --> 00:44:58.696
A criminal lawyer?

832
00:44:58.739 --> 00:45:00.654
I am.

833
00:45:00.698 --> 00:45:02.917
What's he saying?

834
00:45:02.961 --> 00:45:05.964
I believe there's a clear issue
of conflict of interest,

835
00:45:06.007 --> 00:45:10.490
and that being the case, we
cannot even begin to proceed

836
00:45:10.533 --> 00:45:12.753
until I ascertain whether
I'm right or not,

837
00:45:12.797 --> 00:45:14.059
by questioning you.

838
00:45:14.102 --> 00:45:15.234
Except it doesn't
work that way.

839
00:45:15.277 --> 00:45:16.365
I'm afraid it does.

840
00:45:16.409 --> 00:45:17.758
If I have any
indication

841
00:45:17.802 --> 00:45:21.109
of conflict of interest
I can object.

842
00:45:21.153 --> 00:45:22.632
And I object.

843
00:45:22.676 --> 00:45:24.634
I object to your objection.

844
00:45:25.679 --> 00:45:31.598
♪

845
00:45:31.641 --> 00:45:33.643
What happens now?

846
00:45:36.037 --> 00:45:37.691
So let's overrule it.

847
00:45:37.735 --> 00:45:41.651
[crowd chatters in agreement]

848
00:45:45.264 --> 00:45:47.179
Barbara: Jesus Christ!

849
00:45:47.222 --> 00:45:48.615
News Anchor: A surprising
turn of events, Harper.

850
00:45:48.658 --> 00:45:50.095
But as the numbers tell you,

851
00:45:50.138 --> 00:45:53.272
right now,
people are clearly voting

852
00:45:53.315 --> 00:45:55.665
to support the judges objection and overrule

853
00:45:55.709 --> 00:45:57.885
the man who is now
holding him hostage.

854
00:45:57.929 --> 00:46:01.193
What does it say?

855
00:46:01.236 --> 00:46:05.806
Well, my objection
has been overruled.

856
00:46:05.850 --> 00:46:07.416
All right then.

857
00:46:07.460 --> 00:46:09.201
It appears that the voice
of the people--

858
00:46:09.244 --> 00:46:14.206
Hero: By a vote of
47,239 to 19,640.

859
00:46:14.249 --> 00:46:16.382
Nearly 70,000 people
taking part already.

860
00:46:16.425 --> 00:46:18.863
News Anchor: More than ten
percent of the people watching

861
00:46:18.906 --> 00:46:21.517
are actually taking
part and voting.

862
00:46:21.561 --> 00:46:23.345
That seems a massive
number to me.

863
00:46:23.389 --> 00:46:26.392
And I suspect that percentage
is only going to grow.

864
00:46:26.435 --> 00:46:27.697
Holy shit.

865
00:46:29.090 --> 00:46:30.700
Stokely!

866
00:46:32.615 --> 00:46:33.834
Take a seat.

867
00:46:40.536 --> 00:46:41.929
What was his name?

868
00:46:41.973 --> 00:46:44.192
The detective who oversaw
the Jeeter case.

869
00:46:44.236 --> 00:46:45.672
Steptoe.

870
00:46:45.715 --> 00:46:47.195
Do you know him?

871
00:46:47.239 --> 00:46:48.457
For a while, I was a
junior in his unit.

872
00:46:48.501 --> 00:46:49.763
Not on the Jeeter case.

873
00:46:49.807 --> 00:46:50.851
Call him.

874
00:46:50.895 --> 00:46:52.287
Why?

875
00:46:52.331 --> 00:46:54.768
What if this guy actually
has a point?

876
00:46:54.812 --> 00:46:57.466
About the judge?

877
00:46:57.510 --> 00:47:00.861
I believe the obvious question
now is are you going

878
00:47:00.905 --> 00:47:04.256
to abide by the order
from the bench?

879
00:47:04.299 --> 00:47:06.258
So you accept this as
a courtroom now?

880
00:47:06.301 --> 00:47:08.782
I mean if you're saying words
like "abide" and "bench"--

881
00:47:08.826 --> 00:47:10.566
No, this is not
a courtroom.

882
00:47:10.610 --> 00:47:13.613
But if you abide
by the ruling

883
00:47:13.656 --> 00:47:16.485
