specific axe to grind.

927
00:49:36.495 --> 00:49:38.018
And that may explain why he's
taken this course of action

928
00:49:38.062 --> 00:49:39.933
in the first place.

929
00:49:39.977 --> 00:49:41.369
Harper: Would this be some
kind of a grudge?

930
00:49:41.413 --> 00:49:43.023
Well, that's exactly
the problem, Harper.

931
00:49:43.067 --> 00:49:44.024
We don't know.

932
00:49:44.068 --> 00:49:45.634
What we do know is:

933
00:49:45.678 --> 00:49:48.898
this morning saw the execution
of Paul William Gager.

934
00:49:48.942 --> 00:49:50.117
Claudine's killer.

935
00:49:50.161 --> 00:49:51.989
Now, if there is
an axe to grind

936
00:49:52.032 --> 00:49:53.773
about a trial being
misconducted--

937
00:49:53.816 --> 00:49:55.775
It's possible that the family
had harboured doubts

938
00:49:55.818 --> 00:49:57.342
about the Gager
verdict all along.

939
00:49:57.385 --> 00:49:59.083
I don't think we
can say that.

940
00:49:59.126 --> 00:50:01.607
Now Josh, tell me, doesn't
this bring us right back

941
00:50:01.650 --> 00:50:03.826
to the question surrounding
Judge Straight's handling

942
00:50:03.870 --> 00:50:05.089
of the case?

943
00:50:05.132 --> 00:50:06.612
Josh: It could.

944
00:50:06.655 --> 00:50:09.832
You do not have the
right to try this case.

945
00:50:09.876 --> 00:50:11.486
Any reasonable judge
would tell you--

946
00:50:11.530 --> 00:50:14.228
No, we don't have to speculate
on what a reasonable judge

947
00:50:14.272 --> 00:50:16.100
would say, because
we have a judge.

948
00:50:16.143 --> 00:50:18.885
And I don't think the judge
will say that my relationship

949
00:50:18.928 --> 00:50:21.105
