from trying this case,

950
00:50:21.148 --> 00:50:23.890
because the case at hand is
not about Claudine's abduction.

951
00:50:23.933 --> 00:50:27.763
It's about you putting an
innocent man to death.

952
00:50:27.807 --> 00:50:29.939
That's the case
at trial here.

953
00:50:29.983 --> 00:50:32.725
So, I say we put it
to a judge's ruling.

954
00:50:34.640 --> 00:50:36.337
That wouldn't stand
up anywhere.

955
00:50:36.381 --> 00:50:37.991
Terry: It will here.

956
00:50:38.035 --> 00:50:39.993
It's not enough to just
surround the house.

957
00:50:40.037 --> 00:50:41.864
Someone has to
talk to the family.

958
00:50:41.908 --> 00:50:44.911
That's why I said
the cousin.

959
00:50:44.954 --> 00:50:46.608
Then let me talk
to them.

960
00:50:46.652 --> 00:50:47.696
His name is what?

961
00:50:47.740 --> 00:50:50.221
Bertinad, right?

962
00:50:50.264 --> 00:50:51.526
Then what is
the problem--

963
00:50:51.570 --> 00:50:53.311
Lt. Elroy?

964
00:50:53.354 --> 00:50:55.226
Hi, Leonard Steptoe.

965
00:50:55.269 --> 00:50:58.229
I was in charge of the
Jeeter investigation.

966
00:50:58.272 --> 00:51:00.927
It looks like you've got
yourself in some situation, huh?

967
00:51:00.970 --> 00:51:03.582
I'm in the middle of a
nightmare, detective.

968
00:51:03.625 --> 00:51:05.845
I'm here to help you
any way I can.

969
00:51:05.888 --> 00:51:08.152
All right, now to start,
there's information

970
00:51:08.195 --> 00:51:11.459
about the Jeeter family
that you need to know.

971
00:51:15.159 --> 00:51:17.378
Come on, you
gotta be there.

972
00:51:21.513 --> 00:51:22.905
Oh shit.

973
00:51:24.690 --> 00:51:25.908
Steptoe: The uncle?

974
00:51:25.952 --> 00:51:27.432
He's dead.

975
00:51:27.475 --> 00:51:29.129
Say again?

976
00:51:29.173 --> 00:51:31.436
His car slipped into the
Tremont Viaduct,

977
00:51:31.479 --> 00:51:33.829
so whatever this freak
says he wants,

978
00:51:33.873 --> 00:51:36.658
it's not 'cause he's Claudine
Jeeter's uncle.

979
00:51:36.702 --> 00:51:38.399
Harper: And it looks
like, once again

980
00:51:38.443 --> 00:51:40.445
the objection is overruled.

981
00:51:40.488 --> 00:51:43.012
Your objection has
been overruled.

982
00:51:44.797 --> 00:51:47.452
I would like to know the
judge's reasoning.

983
00:51:47.495 --> 00:51:51.412
Do you always give a reason
when you're on the bench?

984
00:51:51.456 --> 00:51:53.414
You've already accepted
one of the judge's rulings,

985
00:51:53.458 --> 00:51:56.243
so that means you accept
the authority of this court.

986
00:51:56.287 --> 00:51:57.679
[deep sigh]

987
00:51:57.723 --> 00:52:00.204
Let's be perfectly clear.

988
00:52:00.247 --> 00:52:04.817
The people who investigated and
tried the Jeeter case needed

989
00:52:04.860 --> 00:52:09.126
and wanted a crazed,
lone psychopath.

990
00:52:09.169 --> 00:52:11.389
And they needed one for a
very simple reason.

991
00:52:11.432 --> 00:52:13.173
See, the killing of
a young person

992
00:52:13.217 --> 00:52:15.175
is the worst crime that
we can imagine.

993
00:52:15.219 --> 00:52:20.180
In order to reconcile this
horror in our minds we need,

994
00:52:20.224 --> 00:52:24.315
we must have, and we must kill

995
00:52:24.358 --> 00:52:27.622
a crazed lone psychopath.

996
00:52:27.666 --> 00:52:32.366
Anybody who doesn't feel
that longing is inhuman.

997
00:52:32.410 --> 00:52:34.629
And it's written all
over this case.

998
00:52:34.673 --> 00:52:36.196
The lawyers, the police.

999
00:52:36.240 --> 00:52:38.329
And most of all the
justice system.

1000
00:52:38.372 --> 00:52:41.332
Every decision they made was
based on their humanity.

1001
00:52:41.375 --> 00:52:44.509
And because of the way that this
shitty system is set up

1002
00:52:44.552 --> 00:52:46.511
they were allowed
to take the results

1003
00:52:46.554 --> 00:52:49.383
of those flawed human
conclusions and couple that

1004
00:52:49.427 --> 00:52:52.212
with a power that really
doesn't belong to them.

1005
00:52:52.256 --> 00:52:55.172
The power to give
and take life.

1006
00:52:58.044 --> 00:53:00.089
You have something
to add?

1007
00:53:00.133 --> 00:53:03.049
Is that really what we're
talking about here?

1008
00:53:03.092 --> 00:53:06.879
The validity of the
death penalty?

1009
00:53:06.922 --> 00:53:10.448
I'm sorry, but for
whatever reason,

1010
00:53:10.491 --> 00:53:12.232
I thought this was
going to be

1011
00:53:12.276 --> 00:53:15.279
about something more
original and substantive.

1012
00:53:15.322 --> 00:53:17.019
Look around
you, Judge.

1013
00:53:17.063 --> 00:53:22.024
Do I strike you as someone who
isn't original and substantive?

1014
00:53:22.068 --> 00:53:23.722
This is about justice.

1015
00:53:25.811 --> 00:53:29.031
Now I want to question you about
the police work on this case.

1016
00:53:29.075 --> 00:53:30.772
I'm afraid I cannot
help you there.

1017
00:53:30.816 --> 00:53:32.470
I am not a
policeman.

1018
00:53:32.513 --> 00:53:34.733
Well then I want to question you
about your interpretation

1019
00:53:34.776 --> 00:53:36.561
of the police work
on the case.

1020
00:53:36.604 --> 00:53:38.432
Would you say that
it was thorough?

1021
00:53:38.476 --> 00:53:40.956
Up to the standards that
we expect from our police?

1022
00:53:41.000 --> 00:53:42.654
Of course.

1023
00:53:42.697 --> 00:53:44.395
It would not have come to or
withstood trial otherwise.

1024
00:53:44.438 --> 00:53:46.266
What would those
standards be?

1025
00:53:46.310 --> 00:53:47.485
Isn't it true that most
serious crimes

1026
00:53:47.528 --> 00:53:49.400
in this country
go unsolved?

1027
00:53:49.443 --> 00:53:51.097
By unsolved, you mean...

1028
00:53:51.140 --> 00:53:53.665
I mean no bullshit myths,
no-no dime novels,

1029
00:53:53.708 --> 00:53:56.668
no phony TV dramas.

1030
00:53:56.711 --> 00:53:59.366
Isn't it true that what most
real police officers investigate

1031
00:53:59.410 --> 00:54:01.542
in this country, they can't
and don't solve?

1032
00:54:01.586 --> 00:54:04.415
Isn't it true that only
18 percent

1033
00:54:04.458 --> 00:54:07.766
of all non-violent crimes in
this country are solved?

1034
00:54:07.809 --> 00:54:08.767
18 percent.

1035
00:54:08.810 --> 00:54:10.421
Motherfucker.

1036
00:54:10.464 --> 00:54:12.292
And isn't it also true that
more than fifty percent

1037
00:54:12.336 --> 00:54:13.554
of violent crimes
go unsolved.

1038
00:54:13.598 --> 00:54:15.295
And nearly a third of
all murders--

1039
00:54:15.339 --> 00:54:17.079
That bears no relevance
to the Jeeter--

1040
00:54:17.123 --> 00:54:18.429
Hell, the most
devastating murder

1041
00:54:18.472 --> 00:54:20.169
in the history
of this country

1042
00:54:20.213 --> 00:54:22.346
the assassination of a sitting
American President in full view

1043
00:54:22.389 --> 00:54:24.130
of the entire country
is still unsolved.

1044
00:54:24.173 --> 00:54:25.871
The Zodiac killer, the
Lindbergh baby,

1045
00:54:25.914 --> 00:54:30.615
Jon-Benet Ramsay, the Boston
Strangler, the list goes on.

1046
00:54:30.658 --> 00:54:34.227
Wouldn't it be stating fact to
say that as a standard

1047
00:54:34.271 --> 00:54:39.101
the police are unable to solve
most crimes in this country?

1048
00:54:39.145 --> 00:54:41.843
The Jeeter case
was rock solid.

1049
00:54:41.887 --> 00:54:45.151
There's not a person on this
planet that can prove otherwise.

1050
00:54:50.243 --> 00:54:52.550
Can you tell me what
I'm pulling up here?

1051
00:54:56.554 --> 00:54:59.470
You don't need me to tell
you, it's obvious.

1052
00:54:59.513 --> 00:55:01.123
Answer the question.

1053
00:55:01.167 --> 00:55:03.865
Well, they're
newspaper clippings.

1054
00:55:03.909 --> 00:55:06.651
Um...articles relating to
the Jeeter case.

1055
00:55:06.694 --> 00:55:09.610
Oh, you're familiar
with them?

1056
00:55:09.654 --> 00:55:11.220
Some of them, yes.

1057
00:55:12.613 --> 00:55:14.702
From the time
of the trial?

1058
00:55:14.746 --> 00:55:19.446
I presume so, yes.

1059
00:55:19.490 --> 00:55:24.451
Actually, those were all
from before the trial.

1060
00:55:24.495 --> 00:55:27.280
But-but you say that
they're familiar to you.

1061
00:55:27.324 --> 00:55:30.022
Could you go ahead and tell
the jury what's in them?

1062
00:55:30.065 --> 00:55:32.024
I'm not quite sure I
understand your question.

1063
00:55:32.067 --> 00:55:34.243
That's okay. I'll answer.

1064
00:55:34.287 --> 00:55:36.202
It's the story.

1065
00:55:36.245 --> 00:55:38.422
The story of Paul William
Gager from the moment

1066
00:55:38.465 --> 00:55:39.945
that he was arrested.

1067
00:55:39.988 --> 00:55:41.773
The loner living out
in the country.

1068
00:55:41.816 --> 00:55:43.514
Uncommunicative.

1069
00:55:43.557 --> 00:55:45.559
He had that odd hobby
of metal detection.

1070
00:55:45.603 --> 00:55:47.387
That thing about building
the rabbit hutches

1071
00:55:47.431 --> 00:55:49.433
out of the roadside
construction signs.

1072
00:55:49.476 --> 00:55:51.217
The knocking out of
the interior walls.

1073
00:55:51.260 --> 00:55:54.655
But most of all, that photo,
that high school photo.

1074
00:55:54.699 --> 00:55:56.657
Is there a single person
in this country

1075
00:55:56.701 --> 00:55:59.225
that didn't find that
disturbing?

1076
00:55:59.268 --> 00:56:00.487
You saw it, right?

1077
00:56:00.531 --> 00:56:01.488
Yes.

1078
00:56:01.532 --> 00:56:04.056
Hm, before the trial?

1079
00:56:04.099 --> 00:56:05.927
Um...yes.

1080
00:56:05.971 --> 00:56:06.928
Did you find
it disturbing?

1081
00:56:06.972 --> 00:56:08.843
I found it disturbing.

1082
00:56:08.887 --> 00:56:10.018
Yes.

1083
00:56:10.062 --> 00:56:11.368
Yes what?

1084
00:56:11.411 --> 00:56:13.544
Yes I found it
disturbing.

1085
00:56:13.587 --> 00:56:16.634
Well, I put it to you Judge,
that you saw that photo

1086
00:56:16.677 --> 00:56:19.158
and you put it together with
all those news stories

1087
00:56:19.201 --> 00:56:22.335
and all the evidence against him
just sorta clicked together.

1088
00:56:22.379 --> 00:56:24.076
But, I mean we can't
forget about

1089
00:56:24.119 --> 00:56:25.556
the biggest piece of
evidence, right?

1090
00:56:25.599 --> 00:56:27.384
That she was found
on his property.

1091
00:56:27.427 --> 00:56:29.081
We can't forget
about that.

1092
00:56:29.124 --> 00:56:31.910
And that little link to the shed
by the side of the house.

1093
00:56:31.953 --> 00:56:33.433
Boy that made sense.

1094
00:56:33.477 --> 00:56:34.956
He was her killer.

1095
00:56:35.000 --> 00:56:36.784
That was the determination
of the jury.

1096
00:56:36.828 --> 00:56:38.612
Hm...working from
the facts.

1097
00:56:38.656 --> 00:56:40.353
Yes.

1098
00:56:40.397 --> 00:56:43.225
The facts that the police
provided to the prosecution.

1099
00:56:43.269 --> 00:56:44.488
Yes.

1100
00:56:44.531 --> 00:56:45.489
But not all the
facts, right?

1101
00:56:45.532 --> 00:56:47.012
What are you saying?

1102
00:56:47.055 --> 00:56:48.666
Well, isn't it true that the
jury never heard

1103
00:56:48.709 --> 00:56:50.276
about his previous
criminal history,

1104
00:56:50.319 --> 00:56:52.409
because you, the judge,
deemed it inadmissible?

1105
00:56:52.452 --> 00:56:54.193
Yes, it's true.
I would not admit it.

1106
00:56:54.236 --> 00:56:55.281
Why?

1107
00:56:55.324 --> 00:56:56.630
For his protection.

1108
00:56:56.674 --> 00:56:57.849
Because he had been
previously charged

1109
00:56:57.892 --> 00:57:00.025
with attempted
sexual abuse?

1110
00:57:00.068 --> 00:57:01.505
It would have
prejudiced the jury.

1111
00:57:01.548 --> 00:57:03.768
But it was sexual abuse
of a man, Judge.

1112
00:57:03.811 --> 00:57:05.247
Of a man.

1113
00:57:06.771 --> 00:57:09.469
A 36 year old man who
he tried to pick up

1114
00:57:09.513 --> 00:57:12.820
at the Sapp Brothers
truck stop.

1115
00:57:12.864 --> 00:57:15.693
[typing]

1116
00:57:15.736 --> 00:57:17.825
Isn't it true that he
was also ordered

1117
00:57:17.869 --> 00:57:19.740
into a psychiatric
evaluation?

1118
00:57:19.784 --> 00:57:21.220
Not by me.

1119
00:57:21.263 --> 00:57:22.526
But the results of that
psychiatric evaluation

1120
00:57:22.569 --> 00:57:25.833
were also deemed inadmissible
by you, right?

1121
00:57:25.877 --> 00:57:27.966
Well, help me out with
something here.

1122
00:57:28.009 --> 00:57:31.099
Would a homosexual man, who's
extremely claustrophobic --

1123
00:57:31.143 --> 00:57:32.840
so claustrophobic in
fact he knocked out

1124
00:57:32.884 --> 00:57:34.581
all the interior walls of
his house

1125
00:57:34.625 --> 00:57:36.844
choose to keep a
fourteen year old girl

1126
00:57:36.888 --> 00:57:39.978
in a seven foot by five foot
shed with no windows?

1127
00:57:40.021 --> 00:57:41.545
Because he must
have spent

1128
00:57:41.588 --> 00:57:43.503
a lot of time out there
with her, right?

1129
00:57:43.547 --> 00:57:45.766
I mean making all those
dolls and the necklaces

1130
00:57:45.810 --> 00:57:47.115
and the bracelets--

1131
00:57:47.159 --> 00:57:48.769
So the size of the
shed is the issue?

1132
00:57:48.813 --> 00:57:51.076
The size of the shed
is not the issue--

1133
00:57:51.119 --> 00:57:52.512
No, on the contrary.

1134
00:57:52.556 --> 00:57:54.558
I think the size of the
shed is the issue.

1135
00:57:54.601 --> 00:57:57.561
No! The size of the shed
isn't the issue!

1136
00:57:57.604 --> 00:58:00.868
The issue is the court
supressing medical,

1137
00:58:00.912 --> 00:58:03.001
psychiatric, and criminal
evidence based

1138
00:58:03.044 --> 00:58:05.090
on their own God
damn personal bias.

1139
00:58:05.133 --> 00:58:07.788
No, that's almost
impossible to substantiate.

1140
00:58:07.832 --> 00:58:09.573
It may be impossible
to prove,

1141
00:58:09.616 --> 00:58:12.750
but it is possible that
it happened, right?

1142
00:58:12.793 --> 00:58:15.666
Maybe, yes, yes,
It's possible.

1143
00:58:15.709 --> 00:58:17.494
If there's anything
else he can say

1144
00:58:17.537 --> 00:58:22.368
or uncover, I'd like
to know now.

1145
00:58:22.411 --> 00:58:26.720
[typing]

1146
00:58:28.374 --> 00:58:30.985
Let me be
perfectly clear.

1147
00:58:31.029 --> 00:58:35.555
I dedicated two years of my
life to Claudine Jeeter.

1148
00:58:35.599 --> 00:58:37.862
I know I did
right by her.

1149
00:58:37.905 --> 00:58:40.778
So I don't have to take
questions from anyone.

1150
00:58:40.821 --> 00:58:41.996
Certainly not you.

1151
00:58:42.040 --> 00:58:42.997
Why not me?

1152
00:58:43.041 --> 00:58:44.303
Yeah, you made detective.

1153
00:58:44.346 --> 00:58:46.000
You traded it all
away for a desk.

1154
00:58:46.044 --> 00:58:47.567
You couldn't handle
the bad guys.

1155
00:58:47.611 --> 00:58:49.656
Now you're trading in your
desk for retirement.

1156
00:58:49.700 --> 00:58:52.572
You don't have any right to
question me or anyone else

1157
00:58:52.616 --> 00:58:55.706
about the leg work we
did on the Jeeter case.

1158
00:58:55.749 --> 00:58:58.056
We got it right.

1159
00:58:58.099 --> 00:59:00.406
[phone rings]

1160
00:59:00.449 --> 00:59:02.190
Yes?

1161
00:59:02.234 --> 00:59:03.670
Darnley: When did the police or the news media release

1162
00:59:03.714 --> 00:59:05.672
the information about
the size of the shed?

1163
00:59:05.716 --> 00:59:06.717
Who is this?

1164
00:59:06.760 --> 00:59:08.501
It's Darnley.

1165
00:59:08.545 --> 00:59:10.285
And what's that stuff about the
necklaces and the bracelets?

1166
00:59:10.329 --> 00:59:12.113
It's not online, okay?

1167
00:59:12.157 --> 00:59:14.725
And in my world if it's not
online it doesn't exist.

1168
00:59:14.768 --> 00:59:17.554
No one said it before.

1169
00:59:17.597 --> 00:59:19.817
Well, was there anything else
that was possibly suppressed

1170
00:59:19.860 --> 00:59:23.690
in order to guarantee a
conviction in this case?

1171
00:59:31.393 --> 00:59:35.572
Wouldn't you be better able
to answer that than I would?

1172
00:59:38.009 --> 00:59:39.532
You're not her uncle.

1173
00:59:42.274 --> 00:59:45.494
I know who you are.

1174
00:59:45.538 --> 00:59:47.409
You better see this.

1175
00:59:52.501 --> 00:59:54.678
Well if I am who
you think I am,

1176
00:59:54.721 --> 00:59:57.071
you really can't
say it, can you?

1177
00:59:57.115 --> 00:59:58.725
That's the bind.

1178
00:59:58.769 --> 01:00:01.598
The judge can't say without
incriminating himself.

1179
01:00:05.950 --> 01:00:10.171
Question, if that guy withheld
certain information,

1180
01:00:10.215 --> 01:00:11.520
who would know?

1181
01:00:13.261 --> 01:00:14.959
Family.

1182
01:00:15.002 --> 01:00:16.264
Who else?

1183
01:00:18.527 --> 01:00:21.226
[typing]

1184
01:00:21.269 --> 01:00:23.141
Us.

1185
01:00:23.184 --> 01:00:24.533
The victims.

1186
01:00:25.796 --> 01:00:27.536
And...

1187
01:00:27.580 --> 01:00:29.147
The perpetrator.

1188
01:00:30.583 --> 01:00:31.758
The person who
actually kidnapped

1189
01:00:31.802 --> 01:00:33.804
and killed Claudine Jeeter.

1190
01:00:39.723 --> 01:00:42.856
Were they able to absolutely and
without question tie the girl

1191
01:00:42.900 --> 01:00:45.467
to Gager's backyard shed?

1192
01:00:45.511 --> 01:00:47.034
Stokely: You'd have
to ask Steptoe.

1193
01:00:47.078 --> 01:00:49.036
I'm asking you.

1194
01:00:52.997 --> 01:00:55.521
I heard the links to the shed
were circumstantial.

1195
01:00:55.564 --> 01:00:58.002
But they thought they were good
because they had him

1196
01:00:58.045 --> 01:01:00.918
dead to rights on nearly
everything else.

1197
01:01:00.961 --> 01:01:02.223
Nearly?

1198
01:01:07.576 --> 01:01:12.581
[indistinct chatter]

1199
01:01:22.722 --> 01:01:24.419
Well, the judge can't
talk about it

1200
01:01:24.463 --> 01:01:26.508
without incriminating
himself,

1201
01:01:26.552 --> 01:01:29.468
but here's how it might of
happened as these things go.

1202
01:01:35.343 --> 01:01:37.868
He may have been
close to her.

1203
01:01:37.911 --> 01:01:39.739
Close enough
that he saw her.

1204
01:01:39.783 --> 01:01:41.088
Not every day
but enough.

1205
01:01:41.132 --> 01:01:43.351
Enough to know how she
went about her life.

1206
01:01:43.395 --> 01:01:45.440
Walking to and from school
with her friends,

1207
01:01:45.484 --> 01:01:47.660
and playing with her
dog in the park,

1208
01:01:47.704 --> 01:01:50.881
and when she was forced to take
her brother to the corner store

1209
01:01:50.924 --> 01:01:52.883
and she hated it,
and you could tell.

1210
01:01:52.926 --> 01:01:55.015
Her arms and legs
in the summer.

1211
01:01:55.059 --> 01:01:57.626
The shade of
her skin.

1212
01:01:57.670 --> 01:02:00.107
She was a
pure thing.

1213
01:02:00.151 --> 01:02:03.850
Slowly he realized he wanted
to possess that purity.

1214
01:02:03.894 --> 01:02:05.243
Hold it.

1215
01:02:05.286 --> 01:02:07.767
Hold it in his hand
like a snowflake.

1216
01:02:07.811 --> 01:02:11.423
Protect it from
being sullied.

1217
01:02:11.466 --> 01:02:13.904
And then eventually he realized that he would take her.

1218
01:02:13.947 --> 01:02:16.950
He would take her and he
knew it was an awful thing.

1219
01:02:16.994 --> 01:02:18.560
A horrible
thing to do.

1220
01:02:18.604 --> 01:02:20.127
He wrestled with it.

1221
01:02:20.171 --> 01:02:21.738
Can you imagine?

1222
01:02:21.781 --> 01:02:23.740
Wrestling with a
thing like that?

1223
01:02:26.438 --> 01:02:28.048
And then he
just took her.

1224
01:02:28.092 --> 01:02:29.789
In that one
simple act.

1225
01:02:29.833 --> 01:02:31.965
Seconds really.

1226
01:02:32.009 --> 01:02:34.185
His whole life up until
then just shattered.

1227
01:02:34.228 --> 01:02:37.623
Like a...like a mirror
into a million pieces.

1228
01:02:37.666 --> 01:02:42.584
But then he saw the
reaction of the news,

1229
01:02:42.628 --> 01:02:47.198
and the press, and the police,
and he was so relieved

1230
01:02:47.241 --> 01:02:49.504
because he realized
he would be caught.

1231
01:02:49.548 --> 01:02:50.505
They would catch him.

1232
01:02:50.549 --> 01:02:51.768
I mean, they
had to.

1233
01:02:51.811 --> 01:02:53.508
He always saw them
on television.

1234
01:02:53.552 --> 01:02:55.989
They were always saying that
they were getting the job done.

1235
01:02:56.033 --> 01:02:57.469
Working day
and night.

1236
01:02:57.512 --> 01:02:59.210
They wouldn't rest until
they found the killer.

1237
01:02:59.253 --> 01:03:02.474
But day after day went by, and
day after day he wasn't caught,

1238
01:03:02.517 --> 01:03:04.171
he wasn't captured.

1239
01:03:04.215 --> 01:03:06.478
And he came to realize that he
was not going to be caught,

1240
01:03:06.521 --> 01:03:09.350
and the reason for
that was this:

1241
01:03:09.394 --> 01:03:11.875
They didn't know what
they were doing.

1242
01:03:11.918 --> 01:03:14.355
Sure they looked like police,
but they weren't.

1243
01:03:14.399 --> 01:03:15.879
Not really.

1244
01:03:15.922 --> 01:03:17.445
Day after day, they
waved him through

1245
01:03:17.489 --> 01:03:19.143
their preliminary
check points,

1246
01:03:19.186 --> 01:03:22.233
and day after day he could
breathe less and less and less.

1247
01:03:22.276 --> 01:03:25.236
Now it might have been that the
abductor began to test things.

1248
01:03:25.279 --> 01:03:27.020
The first time that they
questioned him

1249
01:03:27.064 --> 01:03:28.500
he gave them
two clues.

1250
01:03:28.543 --> 01:03:31.982
Now, they weren't easy,
but they weren't hard.

1251
01:03:32.025 --> 01:03:33.679
Nothing came of it.

1252
01:03:33.722 --> 01:03:35.246
So the next time
he made it easier.

1253
01:03:35.289 --> 01:03:36.900
Obvious even.

1254
01:03:36.943 --> 01:03:38.815
Didn't matter, they didn't
follow up on that either.

1255
01:03:38.858 --> 01:03:41.208
So finally he mailed in an
anonymous confession.

1256
01:03:41.252 --> 01:03:43.863
He even included some
of his own DNA.

1257
01:03:43.907 --> 01:03:45.865
But the police lost it.

1258
01:03:45.909 --> 01:03:47.911
Now if you can
believe this:

1259
01:03:47.954 --> 01:03:50.827
They were actually in the yard
where she was being kept.

1260
01:03:50.870 --> 01:03:52.480
They were right there.

1261
01:03:52.524 --> 01:03:54.831
All they had to do was walk the
three extra feet but...

1262
01:03:54.874 --> 01:03:57.050
gosh they just couldn't
bring themselves to do it.

1263
01:03:57.094 --> 01:03:59.096
They would have found
her if they had.

1264
01:03:59.139 --> 01:04:01.402
And once he realized
how lousy it all was,

1265
01:04:01.446 --> 01:04:02.664
that the conclusion
was inevitable.

1266
01:04:02.708 --> 01:04:04.144
He would have
to kill her.

1267
01:04:04.188 --> 01:04:05.885
He would have to
kill the girl.

1268
01:04:05.929 --> 01:04:08.670
That would be the only way
that they could catch him.

1269
01:04:08.714 --> 01:04:11.195
Once they had the body, once
they had the evidence

1270
01:04:11.238 --> 01:04:12.936
then they would
need to catch him.

1271
01:04:12.979 --> 01:04:15.764
And once they caught him they
would put him to death

1272
01:04:15.808 --> 01:04:17.244
because that's the only
thing that should happen

1273
01:04:17.288 --> 01:04:18.767
to somebody like him.

1274
01:04:18.811 --> 01:04:21.292
Someone like him that
would do a thing like that

1275
01:04:21.335 --> 01:04:24.295
to somebody like her
deserves to die.

1276
01:04:26.514 --> 01:04:29.082
So he killed her, and once
he began to reckon

1277
01:04:29.126 --> 01:04:32.477
with the real moral realities
of the situation,

1278
01:04:32.520 --> 01:04:34.218
he tipped off
the police.

1279
01:04:34.261 --> 01:04:36.263
The police came and they
collected the body,

1280
01:04:36.307 --> 01:04:38.004
and they collected
the evidence,

1281
01:04:38.048 --> 01:04:39.919
and after that they got
everything wrong.

1282
01:04:39.963 --> 01:04:41.616
They accused Paul
William Gager.

1283
01:04:41.660 --> 01:04:44.271
Paul William Gager, just because
she was on his property.

1284
01:04:44.315 --> 01:04:45.925
And because of the
rabbit hutch's

1285
01:04:45.969 --> 01:04:47.796
made out of
construction signs.

1286
01:04:47.840 --> 01:04:51.713
And of course that
God damn photo.

1287
01:04:51.757 --> 01:04:54.325
And that's what the
cable news ran with.

1288
01:04:54.368 --> 01:04:56.936
That-that photo for
four days straight.

1289
01:04:56.980 --> 01:04:59.156
Every headline.

1290
01:04:59.199 --> 01:05:00.635
And by the time they
were finished with him,

1291
01:05:00.679 --> 01:05:01.985
the whole country
knew that he did it.

1292
01:05:02.028 --> 01:05:04.378
The trial, that was
only a formality.

1293
01:05:04.422 --> 01:05:09.427
All that was left was for you to
preside over the execution.

1294
01:05:10.950 --> 01:05:12.952
Yes.

1295
01:05:12.996 --> 01:05:17.696
I am the prosecution's final and
most irrefutable proof

1296
01:05:17.739 --> 01:05:20.786
that you killed an
innocent man.

1297
01:05:27.662 --> 01:05:29.751
I killed Claudine Jeeter.

1298
01:05:29.795 --> 01:05:30.883
There's not a single
thing you can do

1299
01:05:30.927 --> 01:05:33.059
that can make
that not so.

1300
01:05:38.064 --> 01:05:40.458
[loud chatter]

1301
01:05:52.383 --> 01:05:56.561
I understand how you have
come to the conclusions

1302
01:05:56.604 --> 01:05:59.607
that you've come to.

1303
01:05:59.651 --> 01:06:04.003
But...You have
to remember...

1304
01:06:04.047 --> 01:06:08.965
that the law is administered
by people.

1305
01:06:09.008 --> 01:06:13.360
And people are
not perfect.

1306
01:06:14.579 --> 01:06:16.450
That's not the issue.

1307
01:06:18.235 --> 01:06:21.803
We both know that
that's not the issue.

1308
01:06:21.847 --> 01:06:26.852
The issue is...what is to
be done with me?

1309
01:06:32.075 --> 01:06:35.861
Well...if there were
a trial--

1310
01:06:35.904 --> 01:06:38.820
Well, I think we can get through a trial pretty quickly.

1311
01:06:38.864 --> 01:06:41.649
I'm saying
that I did it.

1312
01:06:41.693 --> 01:06:45.175
I mean I've got all the
proof to back it up.

1313
01:06:45.218 --> 01:06:49.179
I'd say I've got rock solid
guilt coming and going.

1314
01:06:51.703 --> 01:06:54.053
There's the question
of intent.

1315
01:06:54.097 --> 01:06:55.750
Let's talk about intent.

1316
01:06:55.794 --> 01:06:58.318
Was it your intention when you
first entered that courtroom on

1317
01:06:58.362 --> 01:07:01.495
the very first day to see
Claudine Jeeter's killer

1318
01:07:01.539 --> 01:07:05.325
put to death if the jury
found him guilty?

1319
01:07:09.286 --> 01:07:12.158
I believed what
they told me.

1320
01:07:19.165 --> 01:07:20.993
There isn't a single
person out there

1321
01:07:21.037 --> 01:07:22.734
who isn't going to
vote to convict.

1322
01:07:22.777 --> 01:07:25.824
And when that happens I will
own the story one way or--

1323
01:07:25.867 --> 01:07:27.260
Carl--

1324
01:07:27.304 --> 01:07:28.305
Carl!

1325
01:07:28.348 --> 01:07:29.915
Shit.

1326
01:07:39.577 --> 01:07:41.187
I need to talk
to you.

1327
01:07:42.710 --> 01:07:44.669
Harper.

1328
01:07:44.712 --> 01:07:46.279
Why did you float
that crap

1329
01:07:46.323 --> 01:07:48.934
about people questioning
the judge?

1330
01:07:48.977 --> 01:07:53.025
And all that shit
about the verdict?

1331
01:07:59.118 --> 01:08:00.554
Kaitlyn, listen to me.

1332
01:08:00.598 --> 01:08:04.341
The story will be
forgotten tomorrow.

1333
01:08:04.384 --> 01:08:06.082
But not who told it.

1334
01:08:10.434 --> 01:08:12.218
Steptoe: You don't get the
urgency of this?

1335
01:08:12.262 --> 01:08:14.046
We're watching it
on television.

1336
01:08:14.090 --> 01:08:15.917
I mean, bring that to the
commissioner's office--

1337
01:08:15.961 --> 01:08:17.745
What are you doing?

1338
01:08:17.789 --> 01:08:20.139
I'm getting authorization to
take over this whole thing.

1339
01:08:20.183 --> 01:08:22.228
All right, technically it's
not just a homicide,

1340
01:08:22.272 --> 01:08:24.535
it's part of the
Jeeter case, and...

1341
01:08:26.058 --> 01:08:27.712
Come on.

1342
01:08:27.755 --> 01:08:28.887
Look, we both know
they are gonna

1343
01:08:28.930 --> 01:08:30.671
want me to take this over now.

1344
01:08:30.715 --> 01:08:33.021
Oh yeah.

1345
01:08:33.065 --> 01:08:34.414
I believe that.

1346
01:08:36.503 --> 01:08:39.550
You know the new
building is finally ready?

1347
01:08:39.593 --> 01:08:41.639
And I'm not gonna
make it in there.

1348
01:08:41.682 --> 01:08:43.945
37 years on
the force

1349
01:08:43.989 --> 01:08:48.646
and it will all have been
spent in this rat hole.

1350
01:08:48.689 --> 01:08:50.909
This precinct was famous.

1351
01:08:50.952 --> 01:08:54.478
Did you know this building
is 120 years old?

1352
01:08:54.521 --> 01:08:56.306
They redid it
in 1960,

1353
01:08:56.349 --> 01:08:59.787
but it was the original
HQ for all of Metro.

1354
01:09:01.833 --> 01:09:03.356
Remember Frank Stoppard?

1355
01:09:03.400 --> 01:09:05.097
Oh yeah.

1356
01:09:05.141 --> 01:09:07.230
Every night he'd be on TV
talking to the press about,

1357
01:09:07.273 --> 01:09:08.579
"We're investigating this."

1358
01:09:08.622 --> 01:09:11.364
And "we're
investigating that."

1359
01:09:11.408 --> 01:09:14.933
'Cause you know,
the 70's were bad.

1360
01:09:14.976 --> 01:09:15.977
They sure were.

1361
01:09:16.021 --> 01:09:17.892
Violent.

1362
01:09:17.936 --> 01:09:20.808
But no matter how
ugly it was,

1363
01:09:20.852 --> 01:09:24.638
you just felt better
looking at Frank.

1364
01:09:24.682 --> 01:09:28.381
He looked...right.

1365
01:09:28.425 --> 01:09:29.643
A touch of gray.

1366
01:09:29.687 --> 01:09:31.515
Always wore the
right suite.

1367
01:09:31.558 --> 01:09:33.691
All the other guys
were slobs.

1368
01:09:35.780 --> 01:09:37.521
Then I realized they
looked like that

1369
01:09:37.564 --> 01:09:42.482
because they spent their lives
knocking on doors.

1370
01:09:42.526 --> 01:09:46.834
Been working the phones,
and chasing down leads.

1371
01:09:46.878 --> 01:09:48.532
Frank was just
a front man.

1372
01:09:48.575 --> 01:09:49.663
They all knew it.

1373
01:09:49.707 --> 01:09:51.187
Including Frank.

1374
01:09:52.666 --> 01:09:57.628
Today...everyone's
a Frank.

1375
01:09:59.543 --> 01:10:03.242
I didn't take a desk because
I couldn't stand the heat.

1376
01:10:03.286 --> 01:10:06.680
I took a desk because I
saw it all coming apart.

1377
01:10:06.724 --> 01:10:08.421
And I wanted to
do something

1378
01:10:08.465 --> 01:10:10.902
that at least felt like
real police work.

1379
01:10:14.253 --> 01:10:19.084
But this...Terrible
as it is...

1380
01:10:24.089 --> 01:10:27.310
Let's start with one
simple question:

1381
01:10:27.353 --> 01:10:29.964
Were there marks on her
wrists and neck?

1382
01:10:30.008 --> 01:10:31.357
Yes.

1383
01:10:31.401 --> 01:10:33.229
What did Stapleton
say about that?

1384
01:10:33.272 --> 01:10:34.447
Stapleton didn't do
the post mortem.

1385
01:10:34.491 --> 01:10:36.057
It's all in
the reports.

1386
01:10:36.101 --> 01:10:37.450
We had Baker do
the post mortem--

1387
01:10:37.494 --> 01:10:39.757
Stapleton's got 40
years with homicide.

1388
01:10:39.800 --> 01:10:41.411
Yes, I know that.

1389
01:10:41.454 --> 01:10:42.847
An experienced pathologist
would have made something

1390
01:10:42.890 --> 01:10:44.283
of the marks--

1391
01:10:44.327 --> 01:10:46.024
We wanted to pick
up Gager anyway.

1392
01:10:46.067 --> 01:10:48.505
Our hero here, just told us the
two of them made bracelets

1393
01:10:48.548 --> 01:10:50.246
and necklaces together.

1394
01:10:50.289 --> 01:10:52.291
If he knows that
and it's a match,

1395
01:10:52.335 --> 01:10:54.598
then he's our guy,
and he's close by.

1396
01:10:54.641 --> 01:10:56.861
That's a very big
reach Lieutenant.

1397
01:10:58.776 --> 01:11:00.517
He told us.

1398
01:11:00.560 --> 01:11:04.042
"Walking with her friends
back and forth from school...

1399
01:11:04.085 --> 01:11:05.522
The trips to the
corner store...

1400
01:11:05.565 --> 01:11:07.480
In the park with
a dog..."

1401
01:11:07.524 --> 01:11:09.700
He had to see her
do all three.

1402
01:11:09.743 --> 01:11:11.484
You saying we didn't comb
the neighbourhood?

1403
01:11:11.528 --> 01:11:14.270
Because that's the
first thing we did.

1404
01:11:14.313 --> 01:11:16.315
No.

1405
01:11:16.359 --> 01:11:17.969
I don't think
you did.

1406
01:11:18.012 --> 01:11:19.927
I'm telling you
right now.

1407
01:11:19.971 --> 01:11:23.975
We combed that neighbourhood.

1408
01:11:25.977 --> 01:11:27.761
No.

1409
01:11:27.805 --> 01:11:30.068
Harper: So, this is the
original Jeeter stuff?

1410
01:11:30.111 --> 01:11:32.592
Tom: I dug up everything we
had from the first day.

1411
01:11:39.947 --> 01:11:41.993
I heard the radio...one
of the police radios,

1412
01:11:42.036 --> 01:11:44.430
and they were talking
about the girl.

1413
01:11:44.474 --> 01:11:46.954
So...I hope nothing
bad's happened.

1414
01:11:46.998 --> 01:11:48.782
Harper: What else
do you have?

1415
01:11:54.005 --> 01:11:56.442
There's a string of older
houses among the north block

1416
01:11:56.486 --> 01:11:59.010
but only four of them
could have sight lines

1417
01:11:59.053 --> 01:12:00.751
to the school, park,
or corner store.

1418
01:12:00.794 --> 01:12:02.883
But none of them see
Claudine's house, though.

1419
01:12:02.927 --> 01:12:05.146
He didn't talk about
seeing her house.

1420
01:12:05.190 --> 01:12:07.192
He talked about seeing
her at the park,

1421
01:12:07.235 --> 01:12:08.541
and at the
corner store.

1422
01:12:08.585 --> 01:12:10.543
Specifically the corner store.

1423
01:12:12.589 --> 01:12:13.677
There!

1424
01:12:13.720 --> 01:12:15.766
Go back.

1425
01:12:15.809 --> 01:12:17.245
Don't get me wrong, there's
not a person here

1426
01:12:17.289 --> 01:12:18.856
that doesn't feel terrible
about Claudine.

1427
01:12:18.899 --> 01:12:21.162
We're all praying
for her.

1428
01:12:21.206 --> 01:12:25.341
But for sure our civil liberties
are being stepped on here.

1429
01:12:25.384 --> 01:12:26.690
Go back.

1430
01:12:26.733 --> 01:12:29.432
The guy in the grey
shirt in the back.

1431
01:12:29.475 --> 01:12:33.305
But for sure our civil liberties
are being stepped on here.

1432
01:12:33.349 --> 01:12:36.700
What's he saying?

1433
01:12:36.743 --> 01:12:38.397
[indistinct mumbling]

1434
01:12:38.441 --> 01:12:39.703
It could be anything.

1435
01:12:42.314 --> 01:12:44.185
Due civil process.

1436
01:12:44.229 --> 01:12:45.796
"Due civil process."

1437
01:12:45.839 --> 01:12:48.407
Who else you heard
lately talks like that?

1438
01:12:49.495 --> 01:12:50.757
Can you cap him?

1439
01:12:56.110 --> 01:12:57.764
Can we upload this?

1440
01:12:57.808 --> 01:12:59.375
Tom: Why would
we do that?

1441
01:12:59.418 --> 01:13:02.029
To put ourselves where
we belong, Tom.

1442
01:13:03.770 --> 01:13:06.077
In a way, this case
has already been tried.

1443
01:13:06.120 --> 01:13:09.254
The conclusion reached and
the punishment locked in stone.

1444
01:13:09.297 --> 01:13:12.126
My life for Claudine's,
my life for Ron's.

1445
01:13:12.170 --> 01:13:14.520
I'm sure none of you
will object to that.

1446
01:13:14.564 --> 01:13:16.087
But applying the
same rules,

1447
01:13:16.130 --> 01:13:18.437
who will answer for the life
of Paul William Gager?

1448
01:13:18.481 --> 01:13:20.352
Applying the same logic,
someone has to,

1449
01:13:20.396 --> 01:13:21.832
because if
they don't.

1450
01:13:21.875 --> 01:13:24.356
You might as well
set me free.

1451
01:13:24.400 --> 01:13:26.314
That doesn't work.

1452
01:13:29.013 --> 01:13:30.841
There really is
only one person.

1453
01:13:30.884 --> 01:13:32.756
One person who had
access to all the facts.

1454
01:13:32.799 --> 01:13:35.106
One person who had ultimate
control over which facts

1455
01:13:35.149 --> 01:13:37.761
were given to the jury, and
one person who had

1456
01:13:37.804 --> 01:13:39.415
the authority to
say "stop"

1457
01:13:39.458 --> 01:13:41.895
in the event that justice
wasn't being served.

1458
01:13:41.939 --> 01:13:43.680
Most of all, the person
who said,

1459
01:13:43.723 --> 01:13:46.552
"Paul William Gager I
sentence you to death."

1460
01:13:46.596 --> 01:13:48.554
That person is
right here.

1461
01:13:50.382 --> 01:13:53.124
He denies that responsibility
because for the first time,

1462
01:13:53.167 --> 01:13:55.082
he's being called out
on an authority

1463
01:13:55.126 --> 01:13:57.607
that he's always so
naturally assumed.

1464
01:13:57.650 --> 01:14:00.392
Up until now he's only ever
supported the system.

1465
01:14:00.436 --> 01:14:02.438
That's a system
that elected him.

1466
01:14:02.481 --> 01:14:04.178
The system that couldn't
find Claudine Jeeter

1467
01:14:04.222 --> 01:14:05.658
while she was alive.

1468
01:14:05.702 --> 01:14:07.486
And the system that
couldn't find her killer

1469
01:14:07.530 --> 01:14:09.183
when she was dead.

1470
01:14:09.227 --> 01:14:12.099
And the system that sentenced
Paul William Gager,

1471
01:14:12.143 --> 01:14:14.754
an innocent
man, to death.

1472
01:14:14.798 --> 01:14:19.063
With one key stroke you're
going to pronounce him guilty.

1473
01:14:19.106 --> 01:14:21.631
And together we can
finally get right

1474
01:14:21.674 --> 01:14:25.243
what the system has
always gotten so wrong.

1475
01:14:25.286 --> 01:14:28.072
Anything else
would be unjust.

1476
01:14:31.031 --> 01:14:34.600
[loud chatter]

1477
01:14:44.610 --> 01:14:49.615
[indistinct chatter]

1478
01:14:55.316 --> 01:14:57.275
Jean: As you can see
from our monitors,

1479
01:14:57.318 --> 01:14:59.059
a huge number of
people are voting

1480
01:14:59.103 --> 01:15:00.713
to convict Judge Straight.

1481
01:15:00.757 --> 01:15:02.454
It may not be
due process,

1482
01:15:02.498 --> 01:15:05.979
but it does seem to have gripped
viewer imaginations.

1483
01:15:06.023 --> 01:15:08.765
[phone ringing]

1484
01:15:08.808 --> 01:15:10.114
Yeah?

1485
01:15:10.157 --> 01:15:11.419
Is there any way to
stop the voting?

1486
01:15:11.463 --> 01:15:13.596
Clog it or slow it
down or stop it?

1487
01:15:13.639 --> 01:15:15.598
We're getting closer, but
I need more time.

1488
01:15:15.641 --> 01:15:18.122
Maybe, but don't you
have guys to do that?

1489
01:15:18.165 --> 01:15:19.645
Not really.

1490
01:15:19.689 --> 01:15:21.560
But we both know
you can do it.

1491
01:15:21.604 --> 01:15:22.953
And right now I need someone

1492
01:15:22.996 --> 01:15:24.171
who doesn't care
about the rules.

1493
01:15:24.215 --> 01:15:26.173
Darnley: Let me see
what I can do.

1494
01:15:26.217 --> 01:15:30.308
[rapid typing]

1495
01:15:38.577 --> 01:15:43.190
[alarm]

1496
01:15:44.627 --> 01:15:49.588
[rapid typing]

1497
01:15:49.632 --> 01:15:58.379
♪

1498
01:16:17.311 --> 01:16:19.792
News Anchor: Some sort of
stutter in the voting process.

1499
01:16:19.836 --> 01:16:21.489
What'd you just do?

1500
01:16:21.533 --> 01:16:23.274
Darnley: I think I
paused the voting.

1501
01:16:23.317 --> 01:16:24.623
Bought you three,
four minutes. Not much more.

1502
01:16:24.667 --> 01:16:26.538
Okay, and if
you could--

1503
01:16:26.582 --> 01:16:28.671
What's that?

1504
01:16:28.714 --> 01:16:30.194
Tech: A source at
USCN texted it.

1505
01:16:30.237 --> 01:16:32.283
It's a neighbour they
found in old footage.

1506
01:16:32.326 --> 01:16:33.676
Lt. Roy: Our guy said
he was interviewed.

1507
01:16:33.719 --> 01:16:36.330
Cross reference this
against our records.

1508
01:16:36.374 --> 01:16:37.636
Tech: Of course.

1509
01:16:37.680 --> 01:16:41.901
[typing]

1510
01:16:41.945 --> 01:16:42.989
Got it.

1511
01:16:43.033 --> 01:16:43.990
Henry David Cole.

1512
01:16:44.034 --> 01:16:45.644
43 Glenmount.

1513
01:16:45.688 --> 01:16:50.649
Six houses down and across the
street from the Jeeter house.

1514
01:16:50.693 --> 01:16:56.481
♪

1515
01:16:56.524 --> 01:17:01.529
[timer ticking]

1516
01:17:10.495 --> 01:17:12.279
I presume this is
when you intend

1517
01:17:12.323 --> 01:17:16.457
that I make the summation
for the defense?

1518
01:17:18.155 --> 01:17:23.116
I have already said this is
not a real courtroom.

1519
01:17:23.160 --> 01:17:25.771
We've not
had a trial.

1520
01:17:25.815 --> 01:17:28.992
No real evidence has
been presented.

1521
01:17:29.035 --> 01:17:30.820
No real allowance
has been made

1522
01:17:30.863 --> 01:17:35.346
for the reputation of
hearsay or conjecture.

1523
01:17:40.003 --> 01:17:41.918
Um...

1524
01:17:45.748 --> 01:17:50.666
It's important that
we all recognize

1525
01:17:50.709 --> 01:17:53.581
when a jury reaches
a verdict,

1526
01:17:53.625 --> 01:17:58.586
and is delivering it to the
court it is doing so

1527
01:17:58.630 --> 01:18:01.502
as the duly elected
representatives

1528
01:18:01.546 --> 01:18:04.201
of the society,
of our state.

1529
01:18:04.244 --> 01:18:06.420
Terry:
He's losing everyone.

1530
01:18:06.464 --> 01:18:09.293
That's fundamental.

1531
01:18:09.336 --> 01:18:12.513
And it's very important

1532
01:18:12.557 --> 01:18:15.603
that you understand
that the um...

1533
01:18:18.606 --> 01:18:20.086
I should start again.

1534
01:18:20.130 --> 01:18:21.609
May I start
again please?

1535
01:18:21.653 --> 01:18:23.742
I don't think you have
time, Your Honour.

1536
01:18:23.786 --> 01:18:26.223
But it's crucial
for me.

1537
